---
/**
 * Both about pages: explains why Leaflet is NOT linked here. js/about.js
 * injects it instead, resolving both paths from its own script url so the
 * same loader works at the site root and under /en/.
 */
---
    <!--Leaflet is deliberately not linked here. css/leaflet.css and
        js/leaflet.js are fetched by js/about.js instead, for one reason: a
        <link> in <head> holds up the first paint while 14kB of stylesheet for
        a section far below the fold loads. See the comment at the top of
        js/about.js.

        The library is vendored from unpkg like every other library in js/ —
        one less third-party host on the page, and the map keeps working if
        the CDN does not. The dist files were checked against the SRI hashes
        unpkg publishes before being committed; local same-origin files need
        no integrity attribute of their own.-->
